{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-copilot/src/project.rs","issuer":"mailto:bobby-scratch","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-08T21:43:20.364443Z","id":"f487737a2c0783e9ad19d41b1152f82b150de4ae00afdaaa0a187130a49df32b","body":{"kind":"concern","summary":"codex -> copilot -> IR sheds 90 structural key paths and most of the text (13,445 -> 3,077 chars); every other adapter round-trips byte-stable. Pinned as loss in goldens/roundtrip/codex-copilot.json; defect candidate, not classified","tags":["shed","demo","defect-candidate","roundtrip","session:claude-code:77642186-b5fe-4a62-9a4f-c01656ed6335"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-copilot/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:23:41.492617Z","id":"34d907f146c4ce77c4d897b2be9b7a2d37ed25f7a0936973a5a1d0b64529e851","body":{"detail":"Copilot records no per-message input or cache usage, only outputTokens; the session totals exist once, on session.shutdown. Alternatives weighed: a session-level usage field in the document would need a new kind version plus derive, extract, every projector and the goldens invariant to read it; dropping the shutdown totals loses ~222k tokens of real spend (the regression the shutdown fallback fixed). The last assistant turn is where the session settles, as Codex settles a round's total on the round's final turn; the per-message output stays on each turn and the shutdown's output (= Σ outputTokens, verified at 1.0.68) is never added twice. Retires known-defect copilot-session-totals-not-on-steps. Projections now carry the totals (copilot->claude writes them on the last assistant message), and the codex/gemini/cursor projectors drop cache_write_tokens, now visible in the round-trip snapshots as lost key paths.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":325},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"6a94b4b74e74d33cb359eeaf52bf9a5c71dcde03bdd6ef1a94c4092d9b74028a"},"summary":"Decision: session.shutdown's input/cache totals go, verbatim, on the last assistant turn's token_usage (the counters no assistant.message reports), so Σ steps = total_usage as agent-coding-session v1.1.0 requires; that turn's input/cache are the session's, not its own spend","tags":["accounting","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-copilot/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:49:26.008381Z","id":"c2b23c18781e006ac43f0a5580e424801829ce442c0a48f227c41b089b2c7e9c","body":{"detail":"Copilot records no per-message input or cache usage, only outputTokens; the session totals exist once, on session.shutdown. Alternatives weighed: a session-level usage field in the document would need a new kind version plus derive, extract, every projector and the goldens invariant to read it; dropping the shutdown totals loses ~222k tokens of real spend (the regression the shutdown fallback fixed). The last assistant turn is where the session settles, as Codex settles a round's total on the round's final turn; the per-message output stays on each turn and the shutdown's output (= Σ outputTokens, verified at 1.0.68) is never added twice. Retires known-defect copilot-session-totals-not-on-steps. Projections now carry the totals (copilot->claude writes them on the last assistant message), and the codex/gemini/cursor projectors drop cache_write_tokens, now visible in the round-trip snapshots as lost key paths.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":332},"content_hash":"6a94b4b74e74d33cb359eeaf52bf9a5c71dcde03bdd6ef1a94c4092d9b74028a"},"summary":"Decision: session.shutdown's input/cache totals go, verbatim, on the last assistant turn's token_usage (the counters no assistant.message reports), so Σ steps = total_usage as agent-coding-session v1.1.0 requires; that turn's input/cache are the session's, not its own spend","supersedes":"34d907f146c4ce77c4d897b2be9b7a2d37ed25f7a0936973a5a1d0b64529e851","tags":["accounting","goldens","session:claude-code:729d6bb8-59f0-4ddf-892e-603372433260","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-copilot/src/provider.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T19:04:25.561902Z","id":"d612ef59a0a03d5dd72c8712824b6bef7b631effd11d8e667a3c5b80b7cd6fcc","body":{"detail":"Re-anchored after the sub-agent message change moved the line (pr/96). Original detail unchanged.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":339},"content_hash":"4d1ca8903faa138b98b34d9363a3e81b5f56c13cf172da19d6988b5cb78c769f"},"summary":"Decision: session.shutdown's input/cache totals go, verbatim, on the last assistant turn's token_usage (the counters no assistant.message reports), so Σ steps = total_usage as agent-coding-session v1.1.0 requires; that turn's input/cache are the session's, not its own spend","supersedes":"c2b23c18781e006ac43f0a5580e424801829ce442c0a48f227c41b089b2c7e9c","tags":["accounting","goldens","session:claude-code:a69c02ae-2421-41a9-88c7-35c5942b4c1f"]}}
